OL,3,AChild abuse trial of snooker champion
OL,4,AGraeme Dott hears closing arguments
OL,5,
OL,6,FJurors have heard closing arguments in
OL,7,Fthe child abuse trial of former world
OL,8,Fsnooker champion Graeme Dott.
OL,10,FDott, 49, is accused of lewd and
OL,11,Flibidinous behaviour towards a girl and
OL,12,Fboy between 1993 and 2010. He denies
OL,13,Fthe charges.
OL,15,FProsecutor Lindsey Dalziel told the
OL,16,FHigh Court in Glasgow that "brave and
OL,17,Fcompelling" witnesses had given
OL,18,Fevidence of him preying upon the
OL,19,Fchildren.
OL,23,APub: 21-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
